From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Let per-app orientation overrides work on the cover

OVERRIDE_ANY_ORIENTATION_TO_USER only applied while the display ignored
orientation requests, which on the cover also letterboxed every other
portrait app (and broke apps such as Messenger that drop their portrait
request mid-launch). Honour the per-app override on its own, so a single app
can be kept in the cover's current rotation:

    am compat enable OVERRIDE_ANY_ORIENTATION_TO_USER <package>

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.smali
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.smali
@@ -17153,10 +17153,10 @@
 
     const-string v5, "Requested orientation  "
 
+    # Onigiri: let OVERRIDE_ANY_ORIENTATION_TO_USER keep a portrait-locked app in the cover's
+    # current rotation without also letterboxing every other app (ignoreOrientationRequest).
     if-eqz v2, :cond_9
 
-    if-eqz v4, :cond_9
-
     invoke-virtual {v6}, Lcom/android/server/wm/AppCompatCameraOverrides;->isCameraActive()Z
 
     move-result v2
